# 0. Method

## 0.1 Two separate ownership tests

This map deliberately distinguishes **production-truth authority** from **capability ownership**.

For every production fact:

> **Who owns this truth?**

The answer must be exactly one production-authority domain. Two truth owners or no truth owner is an architecture defect.

For every capability:

> **Which subsystem/domain is responsible for implementing, validating, compiling, coordinating, reviewing, or reproducing it?**

A capability boundary may coordinate multiple authority domains without becoming the owner of the production facts it validates.

The governing distinction is:

```text
production authority
        ≠
capability owner
        ≠
coordination boundary
        ≠
execution boundary
```

## 0.2 Status vocabulary

```text
IMPLEMENTED
    Exists, is gated, and is proven within the published M14 baseline scope.

IMPLEMENTED — EXTEND
    Real implementation exists, but Architecture v1.6 requires it to accept or
    coordinate additional production-world concepts.

DEFINED — UNIMPLEMENTED
    Architecture defines the authority/lifecycle/failure semantics strongly enough
    to implement without inventing core product meaning, but no implementation exists.

DEFINED — DESIGN REQUIRED
    Architecture defines the boundary and invariants, but the persistent schema,
    exact format, evaluator, or algorithm still requires deliberate design.

EXECUTION-ONLY — UNIMPLEMENTED
    A downstream candidate/execution capability is legitimate but absent; it owns
    no production truth and must remain below the adoption boundary.

FUTURE DOMAIN
    Deliberately deferred. Architecture reserves the boundary but does not make it
    a near-term implementation requirement.
```

## 0.3 Evidence discipline

- Every `IMPLEMENTED` or `IMPLEMENTED — EXTEND` claim is pinned to the published M14 implementation baseline or an explicit predecessor milestone, not inferred from Architecture v1.6 alone.
- Milestone/source anchors identify the implemented precedent or extension seam.
- `DEFINED — UNIMPLEMENTED` and `DEFINED — DESIGN REQUIRED` rows cite the Architecture v1.6 section and/or binding APR that owns the contract.
- A principle being binding does **not** make a missing integration `IMPLEMENTED`.
- Execution or candidate-generation techniques are never promoted to authority merely because their behavior is useful.
- This map awards no milestone number and freezes no future table/schema/format names.

## 0.4 Register companion status

Architecture Pattern Register v2.5 preserves APR-100 through APR-124 and adds two editorial-resolution/materialization laws after the existing preservation perimeter:

```text
APR-105  test capability reuse/adaptation before inventing new subsystem machinery
APR-106  preserve shared-subset semantics across adapters/generalizations
APR-107  delta realization/correction as downstream execution
APR-108  explicit change + preservation contracts
APR-109  compiled task/agent context remains non-authoritative
APR-110  mutable discovery freezes before production/history depends on it
APR-111  operation status and domain verdict remain separate typed outcomes
APR-121  explicit media-preservation classes orthogonal to production-property preservation
APR-122  immutable approved-source media + exact temporal addressing for editorial decisions
APR-123  playback/proxy media remain non-authoritative representations
APR-124  editorial/conform authority compiles to executor syntax rather than being defined by it
APR-125  editorial meaning resolves deterministically before materialization
APR-126  preservation conform and composition rendering remain replaceable execution modes beneath one resolved edit
```

These patterns add **no new production-truth authority domain**. They refine capability design, execution, automation/context projection, certification, review semantics, and the future editorial/finishing preservation perimeter.

