# 1. Ownership domains

## 1.1 Production-truth authority domains

Only these domains own canonical production facts.

| ID | Authority domain | Owns | Does not own |
|---|---|---|---|
| A1 | Semantic / story authority | who/what exists; narrative facts; Entity revisions; story-meaning relationships; canonical narrative topology | renderer implementation; physical representation bytes |
| A2 | World-state / continuity authority | persistent story-time facts; boundary transitions; effective state at narrative position | approved appearance; local performance timing |
| A3 | Visual identity authority | approved continuity-critical appearance identity | world placement; physical representation identity |
| A4 | Spatial / cinematic authority | reusable world-space facts; continuity-significant placement/trajectory; camera; staging/blocking | mesh/representation bytes; local articulation |
| A5 | Production-realization authority | Production Objects/Revisions; reusable physical/look/rig/etc. realizations; representations; consumption closure | story identity; world placement |
| A6 | Composition / instance authority | reusable assemblies; durable addressable occurrence identity; composition-owned placement/configuration; nested composition membership | persistent state on occurrences; higher spatial truth |
| A7 | Performance authority | local time-varying pose/articulation/deformation/expression; explicitly assigned non-spatial trajectories; Shot-relative event timing | semantic identity; persistent downstream state |
| A8 | Physical-relationship authority | support/contact/attachment/containment/grounding facts and their production status | simulation outcome merely because it was produced |

## 1.2 Capability and coordination boundaries

These boundaries own operations, validation, derived artifacts, or historical procedures. They are **not additional production-truth authorities**.

| ID | Capability boundary | Responsible for | Must not become |
|---|---|---|---|
| C1 | Shot resolution & capture | coherent current resolution, readiness, immutable ShotRevision capture | an independent source of semantic/world/spatial truth |
| C2 | Publication/readiness coordination | cross-domain publication checks, Composition↔Spatial binding validation, revision-substitution compatibility verdicts | owner of either side of the contract it validates |
| C3 | Observation compilation | deterministic derivation of renderer-facing observation specifications from captured authority | production-world identity |
| C4 | Execution / materialization | execution adapters, runtime identity, transport, materialization, output import, execution-only compatibility views | canonical film state |
| C5 | Take / review / approval | candidate Take identity, approval/rejection, Shot canon pointer, consequence/promotion review surfaces | automatic owner of world state or reusable production assets |
| C6 | Historical reproducibility | captured-graph reads, Exact Rerun isolation, recovery, fail-closed historical validation | current-state reinterpretation of history |
| C7 | Candidate-world ingestion | candidate extraction/matching/evidence packaging and domain-granular adoption workflow | authority merely because reconstruction/import succeeded |

