# 2. Who owns this truth

Rows intentionally separate facts that are often conflated.

| Production fact or derived result | Owner / boundary |
|---|---|
| Eva exists as the selected story entity revision | **A1** semantic/story |
| Eva has a forehead cut | **A2** world-state/continuity |
| The cut persists after the applicable boundary | **A2** world-state/continuity |
| The cut appears at 3100 ms inside a Shot | **A7** performance timing; **A2** owns any adopted persistent terminal state |
| What the cut is approved to look like | **A3** visual identity |
| The reusable makeup/geometry/texture realization used to depict the cut | **A5** production realization |
| Eva's exact reusable body/face realization | **A5** production realization |
| Where Eva stands in the persistent world | **A4** spatial |
| Eva's continuity-significant root trajectory | **A4** spatial |
| Eva's explicitly assigned local/non-continuity trajectory | **A7** performance, only where no higher A4 contract owns it |
| Eva's local pose/deformation/expression | **A7** performance |
| `chair-07` exists as one durable addressable occurrence | **A6** composition/instance |
| `chair-07` is the durable subject for persistent state because it is instance-bound | **A6** owns occurrence identity; **A2** owns the state applied to that subject; APR-100 prevents duplicate subjects |
| `chair-07` is fallen | **A2** world-state |
| Which Production Revision realizes `chair-07` in a published composition | **A6** composition pins the reference; **A5** owns the referenced revision itself |
| Compatibility verdict for substituting Chair Revision 3 for Revision 2 | **C2** coordination result under APR-104; it does not become a new production authority |
| Exact Composition Revision ↔ SpatialWorldRevision binding | underlying facts remain **A6 + A4**; the binding contract is validated/coordinated by **C2** under APR-101 |
| Authority-bound desk transform | **A4** spatial; any representation-local transform is downstream materialization |
| Decorative-lamp arrangement owned only by the reusable set | **A6** composition |
| Bulk/procedural placement rule | **A6** composition |
| Camera focal length and Shot camera path | **A4** cinematic |
| Depth/mask/structural observation given to an executor | **C3** derived observation; no production truth ownership |
| Generated/rendered video bytes | **C4** execution output; imported as a **C5** Take candidate |
| Approval of a Take as the Shot's canon | **C5** owns the approval/canon record; it does not thereby adopt generated world-state consequences |
| Future editorial trim/order/transition/placement decision over approved Takes | **FUTURE EDITORIAL AUTHORITY — DESIGN REQUIRED**; it must reference exact approved source media, resolve meaning-bearing choices deterministically, and cannot be inferred from C4 commands or C5 approval alone |
| Playback proxy for an approved Take | **C4** derived representation/evidence; no production/editorial truth ownership |
| Media-preservation class and selected conform/composition materialization mode | **C4** execution/provenance result under APR-121/126; neither proves editorial or production-property correctness |
| Exact source/output lineage of a materialized edit/delivery | **C6/C4** historical/execution provenance over future editorial authority; lineage does not become the editorial decision itself |
| A distinctive generated prop appearing only in a Take | candidate only; becomes **A5/A6** only through explicit promotion/publication/adoption |
| Simulation predicts a lamp fall | candidate/execution evidence only; **A8/A2/A7** change only after explicit adoption in the relevant domain |
| `lamp-main supported_by desk-main` | **A8** physical relationship |
| Reconstructed label suggesting an existing occurrence match | **C7** candidate evidence; actual identity remains **A1/A6** after review |
| Confidence score on a candidate | evidence only; owns no production truth |
| Human-readable `22:05` annotation | annotation only; canonical ordering remains **A1** topology |
| What historical Shot 22 actually used | **C6** reads immutable captured history; the captured facts remain the exact historical A1–A8 identities |
| Whether Shot 22 can rerun today | **C6** historical readiness; any compatibility materialization is **C4** execution-only |

