# 3. Current implementation baseline

All implementation claims below are scoped to the published milestone baseline:

```text
M14 @ 89298e793c651e9e8b9164912c76e3595867a60a
tree 3c4fec0bdb11732f0c77c22acc65d3ba882df393
```

The existing vertical spine provides:

```text
M1–M5   storage/blob identity, provenance assets, Shot/Generation history,
        durable execution lifecycle, candidate Takes, approval/rejection

M6/M7   semantic identity, narrative topology, random-access continuity state,
        controlled relations, coherent capture, Exact Rerun isolation

M8      approved visual identity and visual readiness/capture

M9      model-specific realization profiles, compiler/readiness, runtime capture

M10A–E  spatial/cinematic authority, Shot spatial plans, spatial observation/
        materialization contracts, derived execution artifacts

M10F    recovery, corruption/fault proofs, historical compatibility views,
        scale/query-shape proofs, source-gate proof-map discipline

M11–M14 reusable Production Revisions, stable Composition/occurrence identity,
        authority-complete reusable-world capture, generalized World Observation
        compilation, retained production-world execution, and real GPU source gate
```

The M14 baseline now contains both the vertical authority→capture→execution→history spine and the reusable-production/world-observation path. The next architecture gap before Performance is durable dialogue/vocal identity plus the first concrete Performance representation; M15/M16 remain separately planned continuity work.

