# 4.18 Cross-cutting construction/execution disciplines

These are not new truth owners and do not create graph roots by themselves unless a concrete capability requires implementation.

| Discipline | Classification | Architectural effect |
|---|---|---|
| Reuse-before-invention capability ladder | BINDING DESIGN DISCIPLINE | New foundational subsystem proposals must first test representation/projection/adapter reuse where plausible. |
| Shared-subset equivalence | BINDING SOURCE-GATE RULE | New generalized adapters preserve already-supported semantics or disclose the behavior change explicitly. |
| Delta realization | EXECUTION CAPABILITY | A bounded correction may derive a new Take from a source Take without mutating either the source or upstream production truth. |
| Change + preservation contract | EXECUTION/REVIEW CONTRACT | Correction success requires both intended change and declared protected properties. |
| Task-context projection | FUTURE AUTOMATION CAPABILITY | Agents receive minimal authoritative context; prompts/context remain disposable. |
| Discovery → immutable snapshot | CERTIFICATION/READINESS CONTRACT | Mutable environment knowledge must be frozen before production/history depends on it. |
| Typed operation/domain verdicts | CROSS-CUTTING API CONTRACT | Completion, production verdict, and evidence remain separate. |
| Profile-scoped qualification | READINESS/EVIDENCE CONTRACT | `qualified` applies to revision × profile × protocol × evidence, never to an asset globally. |
| Cheap-before-expensive qualification | PRODUCTION-ECONOMICS DISCIPLINE | Use the cheapest sufficient evidence to falsify a requirement before costly execution. |
| Attempt-delta lineage | EXECUTION/REVIEW DISCIPLINE | Preserve prior attempts and record the exact intentional change. |
| Candidate/select separation | REVIEW/EDITORIAL DISCIPLINE | Raw outputs never become editorial inputs without explicit approval/select. |
| State over variant cross-products | AUTHORITY DISCIPLINE | Independent persistent facts stay composable state; variants are realization packages, not replacement identity. |
| Production-vs-media preservation separation | EDITORIAL/EXECUTION DISCIPLINE | Property preservation and media handling are orthogonal claims; neither substitutes for the other. |
| Immutable approved-source addressing | EDITORIAL/HISTORY DISCIPLINE | Future edit decisions resolve exact approved Take/source/time ranges; trims/reorders never mutate source Takes. |
| Proxy/source separation | EXECUTION/UI DISCIPLINE | Playback proxies may change without changing source identity or edit meaning. |
| Editorial authority → conform compiler | EXECUTION BOUNDARY DISCIPLINE | FFmpeg/NLE/interchange syntax is derived execution provenance, not the editorial decision. |

