# 5. Authority-seam audit

The audit below tests truth ownership separately from coordination responsibility.

| Seam | Potential confusion | Resolution | Truth owner(s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Injury appearance vs physical realization | one visible result appears to be one fact | approved appearance and physical realization are distinct facts | A3 / A5 |
| Stateful `chair-07` | composition identity vs world state | A6 owns occurrence identity; A2 owns state targeting that one durable subject; APR-100 forbids duplicate subjects | A6 identity; A2 state |
| Composition ↔ Spatial binding | coordinator mistaken for third authority | C2 validates one exact A6↔A4 binding; C2 owns no placement truth | A6 + A4 |
| Revision substitution | compatibility verdict mistaken for new asset authority | C2 produces verdict; A5 owns revisions; consuming authorities retain their facts | A5 plus relevant consumer authority |
| Publication vs qualification | one global “locked” state hides scope | A5 owns published revision; C2/C5 own profile-scoped qualification evidence/verdict; current-use selection remains separate | A5 + C2/C5 |
| Reference evidence vs visual truth | image attachment treated as all-property authority | adopted property-scoped claim constrains existing owner; reference itself remains evidence | A3 or other owning property authority |
| Raw candidate vs edit/select | file existence mistaken for production acceptance | C5 approval/select controls downstream editorial consumption | C5 |
| Approved source vs editorial decision | Take approval mistaken for the edit itself | C5 selects source eligibility; future editorial authority owns trims/order/sequence decisions over exact source ranges | C5 + future editorial domain |
| Proxy vs authoritative source | playback/transcode convenience treated as the source | C4 proxy remains derived; future edit resolves retained approved source unless explicit re-adoption creates new source identity | C4 + future editorial domain |
| Media preservation vs production preservation | “lossless” media handling treated as proof that the right film properties were preserved | APR-121 keeps media class separate from property-level preservation/review | C4 evidence + owning production authorities |
| Editorial decision vs conform command | FFmpeg/NLE syntax treated as the edit | authoritative edit compiles to executor plan; syntax is retained provenance only | future editorial domain + C4 |
| Character trajectory | A4 and A7 both appear able to own motion | continuity-significant/root/world placement stays A4; explicitly assigned local/non-spatial motion is A7 | A4 or A7, never both for the same fact |
| Intra-Shot event vs persistent state | one event appears to own both timing and downstream truth | A7 owns Shot-relative timing; A2 owns persistent terminal/downstream state; APR-102 requires agreement | A7 timing / A2 state |
| Shot-start event | duplicate time-zero event vs boundary state | canonical Shot/start transition owns state; redundant event is invalid | A2 |
| Authority-bound instance placement | composition transform vs spatial transform | A4 owns placement; A6 representation transform must agree/derive | A4 |
| Historical representation on current executor | compatibility view appears to replace history | C4 translation is execution-only; C6 reads immutable captured source | no new truth owner |
| Human clock labels | label appears to become chronology | canonical narrative topology remains A1 | A1 |
| Candidate confidence | score appears to decide truth | confidence only prioritizes review; adoption remains explicit | none until relevant A-domain adopts |

**Audit verdict:** no unresolved two-owner or no-owner production fact remains in the accepted pressure-test scope.

