# 7. Handoff to the Gap & Dependency Graph

The Gap & Dependency Graph should consume the following dependency facts without assigning milestone numbers yet:

```text
1. Production Revision → Composition → stable occurrence identity →
   instance-bound state/spatial continuity → Shot-resolution extension.

2. Composition ↔ Spatial binding requires minimal Composition capability plus the
   already-implemented spatial authority; it does not require every A5 feature first.

3. APR-103 stable occurrence identity is required before persistent state can safely
   survive Composition Revision evolution.

4. APR-104 compatibility gates later reusable-revision substitution; it is not required
   merely to create the first immutable Production Revision.

5. Intra-Shot persistent changes split into A7 timing and A2 terminal state.
   The A2 side depends on APR-100 durable authority subjects; capture requires APR-102 agreement.

6. Dialogue semantics (A1) → Vocal Performance (A7) → optional derived alignment →
   dialogue-bound Facial Performance (A7) is the required authority direction for production-grade lip sync.

7. Exact Performance temporal mapping is a co-prerequisite of both Vocal Performance and
   body/facial Performance; broad Sound Post is not.

8. The World Observation Compiler is implemented for the M14 production-world slice and
   remains the downstream execution boundary; later Performance properties extend it rather
   than moving authority into executor-specific controls.

9. Review-side consequence adoption, generated-detail promotion, and QC depend on their
   upstream authorities but do not depend on one another.

10. Candidate-world ingestion is an independent candidate-source branch and must not block
    the dialogue/performance program.

11. Delta realization/correction is downstream of captured authority and the property-level
    preservation contract; it must not become a new production-truth owner.

12. Generalized adapter/compiler work must carry an explicit shared-subset equivalence proof
    wherever a predecessor path already defines supported semantics.

13. Task-context compilation and live capability discovery remain future operational/context
    capabilities unless a concrete authorized milestone requires them; they do not reorder the
    authority program.

14. Future editorial/conform design begins only after explicit Take approval/select and must co-design
    exact source-media/timebase addressing, deterministic resolution of meaning-bearing editorial choices,
    proxy/source separation, media-preservation classes, conform/composition/mixed materialization planning,
    and delivery lineage without assigning executor syntax or renderer behavior editorial authority.
```

The next unresolved filmmaker-complete design slice on the current roadmap remains the **Performance / Dialogue co-design family**. The dependency graph should also add a separate future **Editorial / Conform / Finishing** branch downstream of approved Take/select, but that branch must not reorder the current Performance program:

```text
Dialogue Line identity (A1)
        +
exact Performance temporal mapping
        ↓
Vocal Performance revision (A7)
        +
minimum body/facial Performance representation (A7)
        ↓
vocal↔facial synchronization + Shot capture
```

A separate future branch must also preserve:

```text
approved Take/select
        ↓
exact source media + temporal identity
        ↓
future editorial decision authority
        ↓
deterministic resolved editorial projection
        ↓
preservation-aware conform / composition / mixed materialization
        ↓
derived delivery + exact lineage
```

This is a dependency handoff, not implementation authorization or a schema freeze.

